  "policy": [
    "DIG SOVL0190=raw100uA,nominal DUT94.667uA after5.333uA tare; actual calibration required",
    "Other fullscale limits do not implement approved overcurrent protection",
    "MEMSTAT/ID/readback/stale data/capture CCxOF/ADC nearfullscale cause invalid window",
    "MATHOF is arithmetic overflow, not an analog clipping detector",
    "Assert DDI_RESET and MOS_EN low then use approved safe shutdown; all EN low at boot",
    "Never infer voltage settled from PG alone; measured rails use out-of-window VBUS/VSHUNT snapshots, IO/SYS require qualified timing or bench checks",
    "3.01ohm improves range but increases equivalent current noise/offset; accuracy not yet bench-qualified",
    "R2: 12 INA228 channels; new ALERT outputs diagnostic polling only (no MCU GPIO); only DIG hardware pulse timing. 5uA +/-0.5% UNVERIFIED."
  ]
